
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
CA = CB [00]
A,D,C are collinear [01]
DA = DC [02]
AE = AC [03]
A,E,C are collinear [04]
FB = FE [05]
B,F,E are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. A,D,C are collinear [01] & DA = DC [02] ⇒  D is midpoint of AC [07]
002. B,F,E are collinear [06] & FB = FE [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of EB [08]
003. D is midpoint of AC [07] & F is midpoint of EB [08] ⇒  DA:AC = FB:BE [09]
004. A,E,C are collinear [04] & AE = AC [03] ⇒  A is midpoint of EC [10]
005. A is midpoint of EC [10] & F is midpoint of EB [08] ⇒  AF ∥ CB [11]
006. AF ∥ BC [11] & B,F,E are collinear [06] & A,E,C are collinear [04] ⇒  EF:EB = FA:BC [12]
007. DA:AC = FB:BE [09] & DA = DC [02] & AE = AC [03] & FB = FE [05] & EF:EB = FA:BC [12] & CA = CB [00] ⇒  AF:AE = CD:CB [13]
008. A,E,C are collinear [04] & D,A,C are collinear [01] & AF ∥ BC [11] ⇒  ∠FAE = ∠BCD [14]
009. AF:AE = CD:CB [13] & ∠FAE = ∠BCD [14] (Similar Triangles)⇒  EA:BC = EF:BD [15]
010. FB = FE [05] & EA:BC = EF:BD [15] & AE = AC [03] & CA = CB [00] ⇒  BD = BF
